$llm — local text generation (GGUF / llama-cpp)

SUMMARY
  Runs a local GGUF language model on the joined prompt (all prompt link
  files plus instruction body) and optional system message. Writes one or
  more completions into texts[].

SYNTAX
  $llm
  $llm[3]
  $llm(model='default', max_tokens=512, temperature=0.7, system='You are…')

INPUT
  prompts[] — primary user prompt(s).
  texts[]   — optional extra context appended to the prompt.

OUTPUT
  texts[] — one .txt link per completion variant.

ARGUMENTS
  model=        — GGUF profile name (externals/llm/model_list.py). Default: default
  max_tokens=   — generation limit (default 512)
  temperature=  — sampling temperature (default 0.7)
  seed=         — RNG seed; offset per variant when repeat > 1
  system=       — system prompt string
  gpu_layers= / n_gpu_layers= — layers on GPU (llama-cpp)
  count=        — variants if [n] suffix not used

REPEAT SYNTAX
  $llm[n] — n separate completions.

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EMULATE_LLM=1 — placeholder text files, no model load.
  LLM_N_GPU_LAYERS — default GPU layer count when arg omitted.
  Requires: uv pip install llama-cpp-python (CUDA wheel for GPU).

EXAMPLE
  @rand_prompt: $llm[3] -> $texts_to_prompts -> @good_quality_image
  Create a prompt for the image model…

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  Yes.
